doom eternal is an intense game and at  times you can be forgiven for feeling a  little overwhelmed by the demon horde  especially there are higher difficulties  so to make sure you're ripping and  tearing in the most efficient way  possible we've got a few tips to get  your slaying started the chainsaw works  a little differently in eternal than it  did in doom 2016 in fact it will become  essential in obtaining the valuable  ammunition you need to mulch enemies you  should be having that thing much more  than you did in the previous title as  now it will automatically charge to one  hip which is all that is needed to shred  apart basic imps and soldiers but you'll  still need to find fuel out in the world  if you want to buy sex larger enemies  like Cacodemons and revenants it took me  a little while to break the 2016 habit  of saving the chainsaw for larger foes  but in eternal you should be pleading  demons every damn opportunity  [Applause]  another way to get ammo if you're short  between arenas or want a few extra  shells and rockets before you leave an  area is to take advantage of the  exploding barrels around you not only  are they great to help ug of enemies  that wander too close to them  but with the right upgrades they can  also be a method of resupply using a  combination of the thicker skin  environment and generating barrels  upgrades means that not only did the big  red barrels drop munitions but they also  respawn and with immunity to their  blasts you can go around shooting and  punching them to your heart's content  until your pockets are brimming with  bullets  it took me a while to realize but both  your frag and ice grenades exist on  their own cooldowns so you can spam both  detonating carnage and freezing blasts  to your heart's content  this can be super useful in moments  where you freeze a bunch of demons to  give you some space only to blow them  apart with frags or to be sure you have  spares to stun any Cacodemons with a  shot to their mouth after a few upgrades  to you'll be able to fire them out  rapidly and get all the bonuses that  come with turning imps into ice cubes or  zombies into a thin red paste  through your playthrough you'll start to  find Sentinel crystals that can be used  to increase your health armor and  ammunition levels but if you link them  in the same skill tree you can get  powerful upgrades some of our favorite  combinations are loot magnet to bring  all those sweet drops to you and  combining quick-draw belch and belch  Armour boost to make the most of every  fiery shot you unleash from your  shoulders  it also means you'll get every armor  shard possible and since you're battling  through a demon infested earth you're  going to need them  rooms also offer valuable passive  upgrades as you come across them during  your crusade  now what room you use may rely a lot on  your playstyle but there's a few  standout ones I could heartily recommend  seek and destroy will allow you to  launch into a glory kill from further  away this is not only great to regain  health but it can grant some valuable  invincibility during the animation and  get you out of a sticky spot if you're  cornered punch and Reve means that you  can fire away with blood punch much more  safely and you're guaranteed to get a  good chunk of health back with each  meaty right hook dazed and confused  increases the enemy's stagger state  which may not seem that valuable but  later in the game where arenas can  really get hectic you'll be glad that  demon you didn't get a tear in half is  still kindly waiting for you to finish  it off personally I'm also a fan of  Chronos strike using your weapon mods in  midair will allow you to slow down time  which is great to assess the situation  you're shortly going to be landing into  or just for maximum cool points when you  land an in air slow-motion headshot on  whatever soldier is below you  you'll visit a1 through the story but  remember you can always go back to the  doom fortress prison if you want to warm  up try out a new weapon build or just  practice things like movement and weapon  switching without consequence all those  imps are locked up down there in the  bowels of your fortress so you may as  well use them for something  doom eternal comes with a whole host of  new movement options available to you  from the outset so be sure to utilize  them it's weird that it feels like I'm  barely on the ground or playing this  game but movement is key to staying  alive and eternal with all the enemies  firing rockets whipping energy blasts or  mobbing you and their numbers you can  get overwhelmed rather easily as badass  as the doom Slayer is he's far from  invincible so agility is the best  defense from fireballs and rocket blasts  so keep an eye out for things like  monkey bars and keep dashing as soon as  you're able to and don't be afraid to  use the super shotguns meat hook to drag  you out of the fray and towards that  lone enemy not all perks are created  equal and some will serve you much  better in the early game especially when  praise or tokens are harder to come by  thicker skin and frag stock ups will  allow you to shrug off barrel explosions  and fling your own munitions much more  frequently and getting item finder as  early as possible will make it much  easier to find future upgrades and  collectables - that is as long as you  keep one Slayer eye on your map it will  help you find more tokens as well as  Sentinel batteries which will then allow  you to unlock more tokens and items back  in your fortress  so there are a few tips to get you  started and do maternal if you have any  of your own be sure to leave them in the  comment section below and we may do a  follow up with even more hints to keep  you all ripping and tearing remember to  like the video and subscribe to GameSpot  for more doom eternal  [Music]
 

